    sidecar documents                                           240
    unclassified outputs                                      2,452

Headline always-loaded surface: 483 tokens (claude, the largest single runtime)
  of which item listing (estimate): 189 tokens; pre-listing model reported 308

Per domain:
  domain                             always  conditional    on demand
  (root)                                435           56          203

Scope and caveats:
  - Counts are approximations. Claude's tokenizer is not published; this report uses cl100k_base
    offline. Use the numbers to compare profiles and to compare before and after an edit, not as
    absolute truth.
  - ai-rulez counts only the artifacts it generates. The agent harness adds a fixed floor of its
    own system prompt and tool schemas, plus per-artifact overhead, neither of which ai-rulez
    can see. This report never predicts a session total.
  - Runtimes are not additive. One session loads one runtime's root instructions file, so
    emitting both CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md costs one of them, not both. The headline figure is
    the largest single runtime.
  - "conditional" is surface some harness modes carry and others do not. For a harness that
    lists skills (see the listing lines) skill descriptions are part of the always-loaded
    listing instead.
  - Provenance hash lines are content-dependent: a blake3 hex digest is incompressible, and two
    digests of the same length tokenize to slightly different counts. Expect a few tokens of
    movement per artifact between two profiles for that reason alone.
  - Listing lines estimate what a harness puts in the prompt at session start to advertise
    skills, commands and agents: each entry's name and description, its path where the harness
    includes one, and 27 tokens of framing per entry. The framing constant is calibrated against
    Claude Code (100 skills measured at 64 tokens each) and is an estimate for every other
    harness. The listing is part of the always-loaded figure and of --budget; always_legacy and
    conditional_legacy keep the numbers the earlier model reported.
  - A harness bounds its listing (Codex: a share of the context window; Claude Code: a total
    budget on top of the per-entry description cap) and shortens or omits entries beyond it. The
    listing lines do not apply that bound, so a very large skill set is an upper estimate.
    Presets absent from the listing table (amp, antigravity, baz, hermes, xum) are not modeled
    and report no listing. Skills written only to the shared .agents/skills tree by agents_md
    are not attributed to a preset.
  - Preset "codex" is not described by the provider DSL, so its outputs are classified from
    their paths and its instructions file is measured as one total with no per-section split.
  - Preset "gemini" is not described by the provider DSL, so its outputs are classified from
    their paths and its instructions file is measured as one total with no per-section split.
